# WATCHER-CANARY per-agentd env additions — the three debate participants.
# These lines go into the SAME ~/rtech-agents/.env the units load (all user
# units share one EnvironmentFile). Per-agent identity comes from the systemd
# instance name: rtech-agentd@<id> sets Environment=RTECH_AGENT_ID=%i, so the
# .env does NOT set RTECH_AGENT_ID per agent — the unit template does.
# See deploy/kboard/watcher-canary.md.

# --- shared by all three participants ----------------------------------------
# NATS URL for the agentd role. agentd reads NATS_URL (rtech_agentd.__main__
# ENV_NATS_URL); point it at the authed coordination cluster for the canary.
NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4223
# Stack stamp — a minted wake frame must be stack-scoped, and it MUST match the
# chatd + orchestrator stack. Required whenever the triage agent is a waker.
RTECH_STACK_ID=canary
# Engine: claude is the real engine (subscription auth via the box's `claude`
# CLI; the units scrub ANTHROPIC_* so no API key/proxy pin interferes). The
# per-agent agent.yaml (agents/<slug>/agent.yaml) is AUTHORITATIVE for engine
# kind=claude, so DEV_STACK_ENGINE stays UNSET for the real trio test. A codex
# engine option exists in-code (rtech_agentd.codex_engine) but wake is
# Claude-engine-only in this slice — keep claude for the debate.
# DEV_STACK_ENGINE=scripted   # offline bus-wiring smoke ONLY; leave unset for real

# --- NAGATHA (triage / waker) — agentd-nagatha -------------------------------
# Setting RTECH_WAKE_ALLOWED_AGENTS IS the opt-in that makes THIS agentd a waker:
# it may mint a wake TaskFrame toward a listed teammate. ONLY the triage deploy
# sets it; a woken agent has no allow-list, which bounds wake-chaining. The
# debate fanout itself is orchestrator-driven and does NOT need wake — set this
# only if you also want Nagatha's in-turn wake_agent tool live for the canary.
# Comma list of agentd-<name> ids Nagatha may wake:
# RTECH_WAKE_ALLOWED_AGENTS=agentd-bilby,agentd-skippy

# --- BILBY — agentd-bilby ----------------------------------------------------
# NOT a waker: leave RTECH_WAKE_ALLOWED_AGENTS UNSET. Engine kind=claude comes
# from agents/bilby/agent.yaml. No per-agent env line beyond the shared block.

# --- SKIPPY — agentd-skippy --------------------------------------------------
# NOT a waker: leave RTECH_WAKE_ALLOWED_AGENTS UNSET. Engine kind=claude comes
# from agents/skippy/agent.yaml. No per-agent env line beyond the shared block.

# NOTE: agent.yaml carries model="claude-sonnet-5" for all three today, but the
# systemd units scrub ANTHROPIC_* and the real engine spawns the authenticated
# `claude` CLI with ITS OWN model defaults (subscription auth). The engine kind
# (claude) is what the manifest pins for the canary; do not add ANTHROPIC_* here.
